Actually, more precisely: if $B$ is analytic, then [1B[0m                                                                           [K[6B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[38;2;124;124;124mp(B|x[2B[18C4[0m[4B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[5C[38;2;124;124;124m,a)$[2B[0m[38;2;215;175;255m⠋[0m[4B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[9C[38;2;124;124;124m is[2B[18C5[0m[4B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[12C[38;2;124;124;124m a [2B[18C6[0m[4B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[17B[15C[38;2;124;124;124mlow[2B[0m[38;2;255;175;215m⠉⠁[0m[4B[2A[2C[?25h[?2026l[?2026h[21A[J[38;2;124;124;124mThe problem asks about the existence of a universally measurable $\epsilon$-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124moptimal selector for a lower semianalytic function. This is a classic result in [0m[38;2;124;124;124mthe theory of analytic sets and measurable selection — specifically the Jankov-[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mvon Neumann selection theorem and its extension to lower semianalytic functions.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124mLet me think through this carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mWe have:[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Standard Borel spaces $(X, \mathcal{X})$ and $(A, \mathcal{A})$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $D \subseteq X \times A$ analytic[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $c: D \to [0,\infty]$ lower semianalytic[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- Stochastic kernel $p(\cdot|\cdot)$ with $(x,a) \mapsto p(B|x,a)$ lower [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msemianalytic for each $B \in \mathcal{X}$, and $B \mapsto p(B|x,a)$ a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mprobability measure[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $\eta_u(x,a) = c(x,a) + \int_X u(y) p(dy|x,a)$ for lower semianalytic $u: X [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\to [0,\infty]$[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m- $\eta_u^*(x) = \inf_{a \in D_x} \eta_u(x,a)$ for $x \in \text{proj}_X(D)$[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mQuestion: Given $\epsilon > 0$, does there exist a universally measurable $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\varphi: \text{proj}_X(D) \to A$ with $\varphi(x) \in D_x$ for all $x$ and $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\eta_u(x, \varphi(x)) \leq \eta_u^*(x) + \epsilon$?[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mKey steps:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m1. **$\eta_u$ is lower semianalytic**: We need to show $(x,a) \mapsto [0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\eta_u(x,a)$ is lower semianalytic on $D$.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   - $c$ is lower semianalytic by assumption.[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m   - The integral $\int u(y) p(dy|x,a)$: since $u$ is lower semianalytic and $p$[0m[38;2;124;124;124mis a kernel with lower semianalytic $(x,a) \mapsto p(B|x,a)$, the integral is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mlower semianalytic. This is a standard result (see Bertsekas-Shreve or the [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mtheory of analytic sets). The key fact: if $u$ is lower semianalytic and $p$ has[0m[38;2;124;124;124mlower semianalytic $x \mapsto p(B|x)$, then $x \mapsto \int u \, dp(x)$ is lower[0m[38;2;124;124;124msemianalytic.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m   So $\eta_u$ is lower semianalytic on $D$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m2. **$\eta_u^*$ is lower semianalytic**: The infimum over $a \in D_x$ of a lower[0m[38;2;124;124;124msemianalytic function on an analytic set is lower semianalytic. This is a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfundamental property: if $f: X \times A \to [0,\infty]$ is lower semianalytic [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mand $D$ is analytic, then $g(x) = \inf_{a: (x,a) \in D} f(x,a)$ is lower [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msemianalytic.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m3. **Measurable selection**: The Jankov-von Neumann theorem (and its [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mquantitative version) states that for a lower semianalytic function $f$ on an [0m
[38;2;124;124;124manalytic set $D \subseteq X \times A$, given $\epsilon > 0$, there exists a [0m
[38;2;124;124;124muniversally measurable selector $\varphi: \text{proj}_X(D) \to A$ with $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\varphi(x) \in D_x$ and $f(x, \varphi(x)) \leq f^*(x) + \epsilon$ where $f^*(x) [0m[38;2;124;124;124m= \inf_{a \in D_x} f(x,a)$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mApplying this with $f = \eta_u$ gives the result.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mLet me write this up more carefully.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m**Step 1: $\eta_u$ is lower semianalytic.**[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mA function $f: D \to [0,\infty]$ is lower semianalytic if $\{f > \alpha\}$ is [0m
[38;2;124;124;124manalytic for all $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$, or equivalently $\{f \leq \alpha\}$...[0m[38;2;124;124;124mactually the standard definition: $f$ is lower semianalytic if for every $\alpha[0m[38;2;124;124;124m\in \mathbb{R}$, the set $\{x : f(x) < \alpha\}$ is analytic, or equivalently $[0m
[38;2;124;124;124m\{x : f(x) > \alpha\}$ is analytic. Let me use the convention: $f$ is lower [0m
[38;2;124;124;124msemianalytic if $\{f > r\}$ is analytic for all $r \in \mathbb{R}$ (or [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mequivalently $\{f \geq r\}$... there are various conventions). The key property [0m[38;2;124;124;124mis:[0m

[38;2;124;124;124m- Sum of two nonneg lower semianalytic functions is lower semianalytic.[0m
